  "reason": "Evidence: scVI n200 (0.520 acc) outperforms PCA n2000 (0.485 acc) as the RNA encoder, and image-only is very weak (0.208 acc). The best single-profile RNA result is 0.520. Uncertainty: We have no data on whether multiprofile + aggregation improves RNA performance, which is a fundamental design axis. This experiment (config_005) tests multiprofile with avgpool aggregation using the best encoder (scVI n200), isolating the profile/aggregation effect with a minimal, interpretable change from config_004. Choosing avgpool over transformer keeps the comparison conservative and reduces overfitting risk. If multiprofile+avgpool lifts accuracy meaningfully over 0.520, it validates the multiprofile axis and justifies further exploration (transformer, multimodal multiprofile). If it does not, we save budget by ruling out that direction before committing to more complex multimodal variants. This is the highest-information single step given 6 remaining experiments."
